  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public Sector Modernisation project - Public Sector Modernization project</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Public Sector Modernisation project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den Liberia Offentlig sektor moderniseringsprojekt syftar till att    genomf&#xf6;ra l&#xf6;nereform, &#xf6;ka effektivitet samt f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;tre personal         administrationen i de sju deltagande ministerierna i Liberia.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Liberia Public Sector Modernization Project aims to improve pay   and performance management in participating ministries, and           strengthen payroll management in the Civil Service in Liberia. The    project will benefit Liberian civil servants by improving             transparency and predictability of salaries and human resource        related issues such as career tracks, grade, recruitment &amp; promotion.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project overall objective

The project development objectives is &apos;improve pay and performance management in
participating ministries, and strengthen payroll management in the Civil Service in
Liberia&apos;

The project will benefit Liberian civil servants by improving transparency and
predictability of salaries and human resource related issues such as career tracks, grade,
recruitment and promotion.
The participating Ministries covered by the project include: Ministry of Foreign Affairs,
Ministry of Finance, Ministry of Education, Ministry of Health, Ministry of Internal
Affairs, Ministry of Justice and Ministry of Information Cultural Affairs and Tourism.
The seven Ministries constitute 75% of the civil servants of Liberia.

Project specific objectives:
To achieve its overall objectives as stated above, the following specific objectives were
defined:
1. Improve pay management in the participating ministries
2. Improve payroll management in the civil service
3. Improve performance in participating ministries
4. Improve opportunities for participation of female civil servants in decision making
positions in the civil service</narrative>
  </description>
